<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF GROUP ONE RACES AT LONGCHAMP.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF GROUP ONE RACES AT LONGCHAMP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of group one races at</p>
<p>Longchamp on Sunday:</p>
<p>Prix de l'Abbaye over five furlongs (1 km)</p>
<p>1. Kistena (ridden by Olivier Doleuze)</p>
<p>2. Anabaa (Freddie Head)</p>
<p>3. Hever Golf Rose (Pat Eddery)</p>
<p>10 ran</p>
<p>Distances: Neck, two lengths</p>
<p>Winner owned by Alain and Gerard Wertheimer and trained by</p>
<p>Criquette Head in France</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 65,876 sterling ($103,100)</p>
<p>Pari-mutuel (to and including one franc stake) Win 15.60;</p>
<p>Places 1.10, 1.10, 1.10; Dual forecast 4.20</p>
<p>Prix de l'Arc de Triomphe over one and a half miles (2.4</p>
<p>kms)</p>
<p>1. Helissio (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>2. Pilsudski (Walter Swinburn)</p>
<p>3. Oscar Schindler (Cash Asmussen)</p>
<p>4. Swain (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>16 ran</p>
<p>Distances: Five lengths, short neck</p>
<p>Winner owned by Enrique Sarasola and trained in France by</p>
<p>Elie Lellouche.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 527,000 sterling ($825,000)</p>
<p>Parii-mutuel: Win 2.80; Places 1.70, 5.10, 3.90; Dual</p>
<p>forecast 45.00</p>
</text>
